 167:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c **** 
 168:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c **** /**
 169:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   * @brief  Starts the execution of a ramp using new target and duration. This
 170:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   *         command interrupts the execution of any previous ramp command.
 171:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   *         The generated ramp will be in the modality previously set by
 172:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   *         STC_SetControlMode method.
 173:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   * @param  pHandle: handler of the current instance of the SpeednTorqCtrl component
 174:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   * @param  hTargetFinal final value of command. This is different accordingly
 175:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   *         the STC modality.
 176:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   *         If STC is in Torque mode hTargetFinal is the value of motor torque
 177:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   *         reference at the end of the ramp. This value represents actually the
 178:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   *         Iq current expressed in digit.
 179:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   *         To convert current expressed in Amps to current expressed in digit
 180:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   *         is possible to use the formula:
 181:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   *         Current(digit) = [Current(Amp) * 65536 * Rshunt * Aop]  /  Vdd micro
 182:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   *         If STC is in Speed mode hTargetFinal is the value of mechanical
 183:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   *         rotor speed reference at the end of the ramp expressed in tenths of
 184:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   *         HZ.
 185:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   * @param  hDurationms the duration of the ramp expressed in milliseconds. It
 186:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   *         is possible to set 0 to perform an instantaneous change in the value.
 187:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   * @retval bool It return false if the absolute value of hTargetFinal is out of
 188:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   *         the boundary of the application (Above max application speed or max
 189:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   *         application torque or below min application speed depending on
 190:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   *         current modality of TSC) in this case the command is ignored and the
 191:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   *         previous ramp is not interrupted, otherwise it returns true.
 192:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   */
 193:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c **** __weak bool STC_ExecRamp( SpeednTorqCtrl_Handle_t * pHandle, int16_t hTargetFinal, uint32_t hDurati
