 350:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   * @brief  It is used to compute the new value of motor torque reference. It
 351:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   *         must be called at fixed time equal to hSTCFrequencyHz. It is called
 352:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   *         passing as parameter the speed sensor used to perform the speed
 353:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   *         regulation.
 354:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   * @param  pHandle: handler of the current instance of the SpeednTorqCtrl component
 355:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   * @retval int16_t motor torque reference. This value represents actually the
 356:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   *         Iq current expressed in digit.
 357:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   *         To convert current expressed in Amps to current expressed in digit
 358:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   *         is possible to use the formula:
 359:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   *         Current(digit) = [Current(Amp) * 65536 * Rshunt * Aop]  /  Vdd micro
 360:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/speed_torq_ctrl.c ****   */
